{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016rD2JXDkDfaYNib8X7EBF5","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n     2→// SACRED GEOMETRY — COMPUTATIONAL GEOMETRY\n     3→// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n     4→// Convex hull (Graham scan), point-in-polygon, trit3d lattice.\n     5→// Orientation test = ternary {-1, 0, +1} — geometry IS ternary.\n     6→// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n     7→\n     8→const std = @import(\"std\");\n     9→const mod = @import(\"mod.zig\");\n    10→const fmt = @import(\"format.zig\");\n    11→\n    12→// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n    13→// COMMANDS\n    14→// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n    15→\n    16→/// tri geom hull <x1,y1> <x2,y2> ...\n    17→pub fn cmdHull(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, args: []const []const u8) !void {\n    18→    if (args.len < 3) {\n    19→        std.debug.print(\"Usage: tri geom hull <x1,y1> <x2,y2> <x3,y3> ...\\n\", .{});\n    20→        std.debug.print(\"  Compute convex hull using Graham scan.\\n\", .{});\n    21→        std.debug.print(\"  Example: tri geom hull 0,0 1,0 0.5,1 0.5,0.3 1,1 0,1\\n\", .{});\n    22→        return;\n    23→    }\n    24→\n    25→    // Parse points (max 128)\n    26→    var point_buf: [128]mod.Point2D = undefined;\n    27→    var point_count: usize = 0;\n    28→\n    29→    for (args) |arg| {\n    30→        if (parsePoint(arg)) |pt| {\n    31→            if (point_count < 128) {\n    32→                point_buf[point_count] = pt;\n    33→                point_count += 1;\n    34→            }\n    35→        } else {\n    36→            std.debug.print(\"Invalid point: {s} (format: x,y)\\n\", .{arg});\n    37→            return;\n    38→        }\n    39→    }\n    40→\n    41→    if (point_count < 3) {\n    42→        std.debug.print(\"Need at least 3 points for convex hull\\n\", .{});\n    43→        return;\n    44→    }\n    45→\n    46→    // Compute hull\n    47→    const hull = try convexHull(allocator, point_buf[0..point_count]);\n    48→    defer allocator.free(hull);\n    49→\n    50→    fmt.boxHeader(\"CONVEX HULL (Graham Scan)\");\n    51→    std.debug.print(\"\\n\", .{});\n    52→\n    53→    std.debug.print(\"  Input points:      {d}\\n\", .{point_count});\n    54→    for (point_buf[0..point_count], 0..) |pt, i| {\n    55→        std.debug.print(\"    P{d}: ({d:.4}, {d:.4})\\n\", .{ i, pt.x, pt.y });\n    56→    }\n    57→\n    58→    fmt.separator();\n    59→    std.debug.print(\"  Hull vertices:     {d}\\n\", .{hull.len});\n    60→    for (hull, 0..) |pt, i| {\n    61→        std.debug.print(\"    H{d}: ({d:.4}, {d:.4})\\n\", .{ i, pt.x, pt.y });\n    62→    }\n    63→\n    64→    fmt.separator();\n    65→    std.debug.print(\"\\n  {s}Orientation test = ternary: {{-1, 0, +1}}{s}\\n\", .{ fmt.CYAN, fmt.RESET });\n    66→    std.debug.print(\"  {s}+1 (CCW/left turn) => keep point on hull{s}\\n\", .{ fmt.GRAY, fmt.RESET });\n    67→    std.debug.print(\"  {s} 0 (collinear)     => skip (degenerate){s}\\n\", .{ fmt.GRAY, fmt.RESET });\n    68→    std.debug.print(\"  {s}-1 (CW/right turn)  => pop stack, not on hull{s}\\n\", .{ fmt.GRAY, fmt.RESET });\n    69→\n    70→    fmt.boxFooter();\n    71→}\n    72→\n    73→/// tri geom pip <x> <y> <x1,y1> <x2,y2> ...\n    74→pub fn cmdPip(args: []const []const u8) void {\n    75→    if (args.len < 5) {\n    76→        std.debug.print(\"Usage: tri geom pip <x> <y> <x1,y1> <x2,y2> <x3,y3> ...\\n\", .{});\n    77→        std.debug.print(\"  Point-in-polygon test (ray casting). Result is ternary!\\n\", .{});\n    78→        std.debug.print(\"  Example: tri geom pip 0.5 0.5 0,0 1,0 1,1 0,1\\n\", .{});\n    79→        return;\n    80→    }\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44d2ecaa-b17e-43c0-bdaa-9bdb8e6b7a9a","uuid":"ed632dd4-0c2e-4f54-9260-11af3f1031dc","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/playra/trinity-w1/src/tri/geometry/computational.zig","content":"// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n// SACRED GEOMETRY — COMPUTATIONAL GEOMETRY\n// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n// Convex hull (Graham scan), point-in-polygon, trit3d lattice.\n// Orientation test = ternary {-1, 0, +1} — geometry IS ternary.\n// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nconst std = @import(\"std\");\nconst mod = @import(\"mod.zig\");\nconst fmt = @import(\"format.zig\");\n\n// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n// COMMANDS\n// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n/// tri geom hull <x1,y1> <x2,y2> ...\npub fn cmdHull(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, args: []const []const u8) !void {\n    if (args.len < 3) {\n        std.debug.print(\"Usage: tri geom hull <x1,y1> <x2,y2> <x3,y3> ...\\n\", .{});\n        std.debug.print(\"  Compute convex hull using Graham scan.\\n\", .{});\n        std.debug.print(\"  Example: tri geom hull 0,0 1,0 0.5,1 0.5,0.3 1,1 0,1\\n\", .{});\n        return;\n    }\n\n    // Parse points (max 128)\n    var point_buf: [128]mod.Point2D = undefined;\n    var point_count: usize = 0;\n\n    for (args) |arg| {\n        if (parsePoint(arg)) |pt| {\n            if (point_count < 128) {\n                point_buf[point_count] = pt;\n                point_count += 1;\n            }\n        } else {\n            std.debug.print(\"Invalid point: {s} (format: x,y)\\n\", .{arg});\n            return;\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (point_count < 3) {\n        std.debug.print(\"Need at least 3 points for convex hull\\n\", .{});\n        return;\n    }\n\n    // Compute hull\n    const hull = try convexHull(allocator, point_buf[0..point_count]);\n    defer allocator.free(hull);\n\n    fmt.boxHeader(\"CONVEX HULL (Graham Scan)\");\n    std.debug.print(\"\\n\", .{});\n\n    std.debug.print(\"  Input points:      {d}\\n\", .{point_count});\n    for (point_buf[0..point_count], 0..) |pt, i| {\n        std.debug.print(\"    P{d}: ({d:.4}, {d:.4})\\n\", .{ i, pt.x, pt.y });\n    }\n\n    fmt.separator();\n    std.debug.print(\"  Hull vertices:     {d}\\n\", .{hull.len});\n    for (hull, 0..) |pt, i| {\n        std.debug.print(\"    H{d}: ({d:.4}, {d:.4})\\n\", .{ i, pt.x, pt.y });\n    }\n\n    fmt.separator();\n    std.debug.print(\"\\n  {s}Orientation test = ternary: {{-1, 0, +1}}{s}\\n\", .{ fmt.CYAN, fmt.RESET });\n    std.debug.print(\"  {s}+1 (CCW/left turn) => keep point on hull{s}\\n\", .{ fmt.GRAY, fmt.RESET });\n    std.debug.print(\"  {s} 0 (collinear)     => skip (degenerate){s}\\n\", .{ fmt.GRAY, fmt.RESET });\n    std.debug.print(\"  {s}-1 (CW/right turn)  => pop stack, not on hull{s}\\n\", .{ fmt.GRAY, fmt.RESET });\n\n    fmt.boxFooter();\n}\n\n/// tri geom pip <x> <y> <x1,y1> <x2,y2> ...\npub fn cmdPip(args: []const []const u8) void {\n    if (args.len < 5) {\n        std.debug.print(\"Usage: tri geom pip <x> <y> <x1,y1> <x2,y2> <x3,y3> ...\\n\", .{});\n        std.debug.print(\"  Point-in-polygon test (ray casting). Result is ternary!\\n\", .{});\n        std.debug.print(\"  Example: tri geom pip 0.5 0.5 0,0 1,0 1,1 0,1\\n\", .{});\n        return;\n    }","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":389}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0164Z6z84tJZm7acmnGJCd13","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n     2→// SACRED GEOMETRY MODULE v1.0 — CLI COMMANDS\n     3→// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n     4→// Main command dispatcher for tri geom commands.\n     5→// φ² + 1/φ² = 3 = TRINITY | Sierpinski dim = 1.585 = bits/trit\n     6→// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n     7→\n     8→const std = @import(\"std\");\n     9→const platonic = @import(\"platonic.zig\");\n    10→const fractal = @import(\"fractal.zig\");\n    11→const sacred = @import(\"sacred.zig\");\n    12→const computational = @import(\"computational.zig\");\n    13→const non_euclidean = @import(\"non_euclidean.zig\");\n    14→const sacred_bridge = @import(\"sacred_bridge.zig\");\n    15→const spiral = @import(\"spiral.zig\");\n    16→const coptic_overlay = @import(\"coptic_overlay.zig\");\n    17→\n    18→/// Main entry point: tri geom <subcommand> [args...]\n    19→pub fn runGeometryCommand(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, args: []const []const u8) !void {\n    20→    if (args.len == 0) {\n    21→        showHelp();\n    22→        return;\n    23→    }\n    24→\n    25→    const command = args[0];\n    26→    const sub_args = if (args.len > 1) args[1..] else &[_][]const u8{};\n    27→\n    28→    // Sacred Geometry\n    29→    if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"platonic\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"plato\")) {\n    30→        platonic.cmdPlatonic(sub_args);\n    31→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"euler\")) {\n    32→        platonic.cmdEuler(sub_args);\n    33→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"vesica\")) {\n    34→        sacred.cmdVesica(sub_args);\n    35→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"pentagon\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"pent\")) {\n    36→        sacred.cmdPentagon(sub_args);\n    37→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"flower\")) {\n    38→        sacred.cmdFlower(sub_args);\n    39→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"metatron\")) {\n    40→        sacred.cmdMetatron(sub_args);\n    41→    }\n    42→    // Sacred Integration (v2.0)\n    43→    else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"sacred\")) {\n    44→        sacred_bridge.cmdSacred();\n    45→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"formula-predict\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"fp\")) {\n    46→        sacred_bridge.cmdFormulaPredict(sub_args);\n    47→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"spiral\")) {\n    48→        spiral.cmdSpiral(sub_args);\n    49→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"coptic\")) {\n    50→        coptic_overlay.cmdCoptic();\n    51→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"trit3d-coptic\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"lattice-coptic\")) {\n    52→        coptic_overlay.cmdTrit3DCoptic();\n    53→    }\n    54→    // Fractal Geometry\n    55→    else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"sierpinski\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"sierp\")) {\n    56→        fractal.cmdSierpinski(sub_args);\n    57→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"koch\")) {\n    58→        fractal.cmdKoch(sub_args);\n    59→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"cantor\")) {\n    60→        fractal.cmdCantor(sub_args);\n    61→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"fractal-dim\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"dim\")) {\n    62→        fractal.cmdFractalDim(sub_args);\n    63→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"mandelbrot\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"mandel\")) {\n    64→        fractal.cmdMandelbrot();\n    65→    }\n    66→    // Computational Geometry\n    67→    else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"hull\")) {\n    68→        try computational.cmdHull(allocator, sub_args);\n    69→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"pip\")) {\n    70→        computational.cmdPip(sub_args);\n    71→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"trit3d\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"lattice\")) {\n    72→        computational.cmdTrit3D();\n    73→    }\n    74→    // Non-Euclidean Geometry\n    75→    else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"sphere\")) {\n    76→        non_euclidean.cmdSphere(sub_args);\n    77→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"hyper\")) {\n    78→        non_euclidean.cmdHyper(sub_args);\n    79→    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"curvature\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"curv\")) {\n    80→        non_euclidean.cmdCurvature();\n    81→    }\n    82→    // Help\n    83→    else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"help\")) {\n    84→        showHelp();\n    85→    } else {\n    86→        std.debug.print(\"Unknown geometry command: {s}\\n\\n\", .{command});\n    87→        showHelp();\n    88→    }\n    89→}\n    90→\n    91→fn showHelp() void {\n    92→    std.debug.print(\n    93→        \\\\\n    94→        \\\\  +====================================================================+\n    95→        \\\\  |  SACRED GEOMETRY v2.0                                              |\n    96→        \\\\  |  phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 = TRINITY                                   |\n    97→        \\\\  |  Sierpinski dim = log(3)/log(2) = 1.585 = bits/trit               |\n    98→        \\\\  +====================================================================+\n    99→        \\\\\n   100→        \\\\  SACRED GEOMETRY\n   101→        \\\\  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n   102→        \\\\  tri geom platonic [name] [edge]     5 Platonic solids (V-E+F=2)\n   103→        \\\\  tri geom platonic verify            Verify Euler's formula for all 5\n   104→        \\\\  tri geom platonic coords <name>     Vertex coordinates (phi-based)\n   105→        \\\\  tri geom euler <V> <E> <F>          Verify Euler's polyhedron formula\n   106→        \\\\  tri geom vesica [radius]            Vesica Piscis (sqrt(3) genesis)\n   107→        \\\\  tri geom pentagon [side]            Regular pentagon (d/s = phi)\n   108→        \\\\  tri geom flower [rings]             Flower of Life circle counts\n   109→        \\\\  tri geom metatron [--sacred]        Metatron's Cube (all 5 solids)\n   110→        \\\\\n   111→        \\\\  SACRED INTEGRATION (v2.0)\n   112→        \\\\  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n   113→        \\\\  tri geom sacred                     All constants as Sacred Formulas\n   114→        \\\\  tri geom formula-predict <val>      Fit any value to V=n*3^k*pi^m*phi^p*e^q\n   115→        \\\\  tri geom spiral [turns] [scale]     Golden logarithmic spiral (r=a*phi^(2t/pi))\n   116→        \\\\  tri geom coptic                     27 Coptic glyphs on ternary lattice\n   117→        \\\\  tri geom trit3d-coptic              27-point lattice with glyph labels\n   118→        \\\\\n   119→        \\\\  FRACTAL GEOMETRY\n   120→        \\\\  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n   121→        \\\\  tri geom sierpinski [depth]         Sierpinski triangle (dim=bits/trit!)\n   122→        \\\\  tri geom koch [depth]               Koch snowflake (dim=log4/log3)\n   123→        \\\\  tri geom cantor [depth]             Cantor set (ternary fractal)\n   124→        \\\\  tri geom fractal-dim <N> <r>        Hausdorff dimension: D=log(N)/log(r)\n   125→        \\\\  tri geom mandelbrot                 ASCII Mandelbrot set\n   126→        \\\\\n   127→        \\\\  COMPUTATIONAL GEOMETRY\n   128→        \\\\  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n   129→        \\\\  tri geom hull <x,y> <x,y> ...      Convex hull (orientation=ternary!)\n   130→        \\\\  tri geom pip <x> <y> <polygon...>   Point-in-polygon (result=ternary)\n   131→        \\\\  tri geom trit3d                     27-point ternary 3D lattice\n   132→        \\\\\n   133→        \\\\  NON-EUCLIDEAN GEOMETRY\n   134→        \\\\  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n   135→        \\\\  tri geom sphere distance <coords>   Great circle distance (haversine)\n   136→        \\\\  tri geom sphere triangle <A> <B> <C> Spherical triangle (angle excess)\n   137→        \\\\  tri geom hyper triangle <A> <B> <C>  Hyperbolic triangle (angle defect)\n   138→        \\\\  tri geom curvature                  K = {{-1, 0, +1}} = ternary!\n   139→        \\\\\n   140→        \\\\  tri geom help                       This message\n   141→        \\\\\n   142→        \\\\  ALIASES: geo, geometry, fp (formula-predict), lattice-coptic\n   143→        \\\\\n   144→        \\\\  +====================================================================+\n   145→        \\\\\n   146→    , .{});\n   147→}\n   148→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44d2ecaa-b17e-43c0-bdaa-9bdb8e6b7a9a","uuid":"de2dcfa3-d51f-4ea8-9858-c3c2d0ea1202","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/playra/trinity-w1/src/tri/geometry/commands.zig","content":"// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n// SACRED GEOMETRY MODULE v1.0 — CLI COMMANDS\n// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n// Main command dispatcher for tri geom commands.\n// φ² + 1/φ² = 3 = TRINITY | Sierpinski dim = 1.585 = bits/trit\n// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nconst std = @import(\"std\");\nconst platonic = @import(\"platonic.zig\");\nconst fractal = @import(\"fractal.zig\");\nconst sacred = @import(\"sacred.zig\");\nconst computational = @import(\"computational.zig\");\nconst non_euclidean = @import(\"non_euclidean.zig\");\nconst sacred_bridge = @import(\"sacred_bridge.zig\");\nconst spiral = @import(\"spiral.zig\");\nconst coptic_overlay = @import(\"coptic_overlay.zig\");\n\n/// Main entry point: tri geom <subcommand> [args...]\npub fn runGeometryCommand(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, args: []const []const u8) !void {\n    if (args.len == 0) {\n        showHelp();\n        return;\n    }\n\n    const command = args[0];\n    const sub_args = if (args.len > 1) args[1..] else &[_][]const u8{};\n\n    // Sacred Geometry\n    if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"platonic\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"plato\")) {\n        platonic.cmdPlatonic(sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"euler\")) {\n        platonic.cmdEuler(sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"vesica\")) {\n        sacred.cmdVesica(sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"pentagon\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"pent\")) {\n        sacred.cmdPentagon(sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"flower\")) {\n        sacred.cmdFlower(sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"metatron\")) {\n        sacred.cmdMetatron(sub_args);\n    }\n    // Sacred Integration (v2.0)\n    else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"sacred\")) {\n        sacred_bridge.cmdSacred();\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"formula-predict\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"fp\")) {\n        sacred_bridge.cmdFormulaPredict(sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"spiral\")) {\n        spiral.cmdSpiral(sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"coptic\")) {\n        coptic_overlay.cmdCoptic();\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"trit3d-coptic\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"lattice-coptic\")) {\n        coptic_overlay.cmdTrit3DCoptic();\n    }\n    // Fractal Geometry\n    else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"sierpinski\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"sierp\")) {\n        fractal.cmdSierpinski(sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"koch\")) {\n        fractal.cmdKoch(sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"cantor\")) {\n        fractal.cmdCantor(sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"fractal-dim\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"dim\")) {\n        fractal.cmdFractalDim(sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"mandelbrot\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"mandel\")) {\n        fractal.cmdMandelbrot();\n    }\n    // Computational Geometry\n    else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"hull\")) {\n        try computational.cmdHull(allocator, sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"pip\")) {\n        computational.cmdPip(sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"trit3d\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"lattice\")) {\n        computational.cmdTrit3D();\n    }\n    // Non-Euclidean Geometry\n    else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"sphere\")) {\n        non_euclidean.cmdSphere(sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"hyper\")) {\n        non_euclidean.cmdHyper(sub_args);\n    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"curvature\") or std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"curv\")) {\n        non_euclidean.cmdCurvature();\n    }\n    // Help\n    else if (std.mem.eql(u8, command, \"help\")) {\n        showHelp();\n    } else {\n        std.debug.print(\"Unknown geometry command: {s}\\n\\n\", .{command});\n        showHelp();\n    }\n}\n\nfn showHelp() void {\n    std.debug.print(\n        \\\\\n        \\\\  +====================================================================+\n        \\\\  |  SACRED GEOMETRY v2.0                                              |\n        \\\\  |  phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 = TRINITY                                   |\n        \\\\  |  Sierpinski dim = log(3)/log(2) = 1.585 = bits/trit               |\n        \\\\  +====================================================================+\n        \\\\\n        \\\\  SACRED GEOMETRY\n        \\\\  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n        \\\\  tri geom platonic [name] [edge]     5 Platonic solids (V-E+F=2)\n        \\\\  tri geom platonic verify            Verify Euler's formula for all 5\n        \\\\  tri geom platonic coords <name>     Vertex coordinates (phi-based)\n        \\\\  tri geom euler <V> <E> <F>          Verify Euler's polyhedron formula\n        \\\\  tri geom vesica [radius]            Vesica Piscis (sqrt(3) genesis)\n        \\\\  tri geom pentagon [side]            Regular pentagon (d/s = phi)\n        \\\\  tri geom flower [rings]             Flower of Life circle counts\n        \\\\  tri geom metatron [--sacred]        Metatron's Cube (all 5 solids)\n        \\\\\n        \\\\  SACRED INTEGRATION (v2.0)\n        \\\\  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n        \\\\  tri geom sacred                     All constants as Sacred Formulas\n        \\\\  tri geom formula-predict <val>      Fit any value to V=n*3^k*pi^m*phi^p*e^q\n        \\\\  tri geom spiral [turns] [scale]     Golden logarithmic spiral (r=a*phi^(2t/pi))\n        \\\\  tri geom coptic                     27 Coptic glyphs on ternary lattice\n        \\\\  tri geom trit3d-coptic              27-point lattice with glyph labels\n        \\\\\n        \\\\  FRACTAL GEOMETRY\n        \\\\  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n        \\\\  tri geom sierpinski [depth]         Sierpinski triangle (dim=bits/trit!)\n        \\\\  tri geom koch [depth]               Koch snowflake (dim=log4/log3)\n        \\\\  tri geom cantor [depth]             Cantor set (ternary fractal)\n        \\\\  tri geom fractal-dim <N> <r>        Hausdorff dimension: D=log(N)/log(r)\n        \\\\  tri geom mandelbrot                 ASCII Mandelbrot set\n        \\\\\n        \\\\  COMPUTATIONAL GEOMETRY\n        \\\\  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n        \\\\  tri geom hull <x,y> <x,y> ...      Convex hull (orientation=ternary!)\n        \\\\  tri geom pip <x> <y> <polygon...>   Point-in-polygon (result=ternary)\n        \\\\  tri geom trit3d                     27-point ternary 3D lattice\n        \\\\\n        \\\\  NON-EUCLIDEAN GEOMETRY\n        \\\\  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n        \\\\  tri geom sphere distance <coords>   Great circle distance (haversine)\n        \\\\  tri geom sphere triangle <A> <B> <C> Spherical triangle (angle excess)\n        \\\\  tri geom hyper triangle <A> <B> <C>  Hyperbolic triangle (angle defect)\n        \\\\  tri geom curvature                  K = {{-1, 0, +1}} = ternary!\n        \\\\\n        \\\\  tri geom help                       This message\n        \\\\\n        \\\\  ALIASES: geo, geometry, fp (formula-predict), lattice-coptic\n        \\\\\n        \\\\  +====================================================================+\n        \\\\\n    , .{});\n}\n","numLines":148,"startLine":1,"totalLines":148}}}
